The browser-process half of the TaffyGo string catalogue.

Grit packs this into `taffy_strings_<locale>.pak`, which the resource bundle
loads and browser-process C++ reads through `l10n_util::GetStringUTF16`. The
only strings here are the ones a C++ surface renders — today, the version
surface labels PAR-SEC-002 requires. Everything a Java or Kotlin surface
renders is in `taffy_android_strings.grd`, and no message appears in both.

Registering the generated pak with the product's resource bundle is the one
part of this that cannot live in the overlay: the repack lists belong to
files Chromium owns. That edit is specified in
chromium/patches/0003-pack-taffy-string-resources.md.

The outputs list every platform locale because the product's locale repack
consumes one `taffy_strings_<locale>.pak` per locale it assembles, exactly as
it does for every upstream catalogue in the same list. `<translations>` is
still empty — the launch language set is `[Open (OD-060)]` — so every
non-English pak carries the English strings through
`fallback_to_english="true"` until .xtb files exist, and the pseudolocales
are generated as usual.

There is no `first_id` attribute here, and that is deliberate rather than an
omission. Chromium allocates resource id ranges centrally in
tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec and passes the allocated start to grit
through its `first-ids-file` argument, precisely so that no catalogue can
choose its own range and collide with another. Adding this catalogue to that spec is an
upstream edit, specified in
chromium/patches/0003-pack-taffy-string-resources.md, and until it lands grit
has no range to give these messages.

VERIFY AT SP-01: that the `first-ids-file` argument is still how a range
reaches a catalogue at the pinned milestone, and what the next free start is.
Upstream files to read: tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec and the `grit_defines`
assembled in tools/grit/grit_rule.gni.
-->
<!-- `output_all_resource_defines` is deliberately absent: grit at milestone
     152 removed the attribute and fails the parse on encountering it. This
     file carried it from an older grit reference before any checkout
     existed to test against. -->
<grit latest_public_release="0" current_release="1"
      source_lang_id="en"
      enc_check="möl">
  <outputs>
    <output filename="grit/taffy_strings.h" type="rc_header">
      <emit emit_type="prepend"></emit>
    </output>
    <output filename="taffy_strings_af.pak" type="data_package" lang="af" />
    <output filename="taffy_strings_am.pak" type="data_package" lang="am" />
    <output filename="taffy_strings_ar.pak" type="data_package" lang="ar" />
    <output filename="taffy_strings_as.pak" type="data_package" lang="as" />
    <output filename="taffy_strings_az.pak" type="data_package" lang="az" />
